Now *that* is a cool idea... though I think much of the interest in these
conducts is having the ability to break them, and choosing not to.  For
example, a recent wishless genoless character of mine spent a long time
debating whether to break a conduct -- it made for an interesting choice.
If I was forced to retain an initial conduct, I'd lose that interesting
choice, which is a bad thing.

I could see the usefulness of a patch that allows forced conducts, though.
One possibility would be to make it reduce the success rate to 25% or
so -- so if you said you'd go wishless and you decide to break that, you
have to waste several wishes.  Also add to the end game screen "you
claimed you would go wishless, but dishonorably broke your word."  (Which,
I suppose, would be in character if you were chaotic... "I lied." :) )



